      "writtenOn": "2020-07-14T08:40:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, so the problem here is, in the \u0027GKI build\u0027 case I want to generate the list of GKI modules. And in the \u0027vendor build\u0027 case, I want to use the list that was generated in the GKI build and pass it to extract_symbol. So, I\u0027m not against having a \u0027MODULE_LIST\u0027 option as you suggest, but we will still need to have a \u0027IS_GKI_BUILD\u0027 flag to make the difference between the two configurations. And the MODULE_LIST variable will always have to point at the GKI module list anyways, for both vendor _and_ gki builds. So, I ended up hardcoding it, and saving a bit of configuration for partners downstream, but I\u0027m open to suggestions.",
